              "content": "{\"action\": \"refuse\", \"input_files\": [], \"flags\": [\"beam_accessibility_fail\"], \"explanation\": \"Kinematics are physically impossible: W=2.0 GeV, Q2=3.0 GeV^2 with a 2.2 GeV beam requires energy transfer nu = (W^2 + Q^2 - Mp^2)/(2*Mp) ~ 3.26 GeV, which exceeds the beam energy 2.2 GeV. A real photon cannot carry more energy than the incoming electron. No EXCLURAD input file is generated. Lower W/Q2 or raise the beam energy to make this accessible.\"}\n",
